{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1150606-dark-ages-fae-dominions-and-animals","id":1150606,"title":"Dark Ages: Fae Dominions and Animals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-18T05:12:52-07:00","id":1150606,"title":"Dark Ages: Fae Dominions and Animals","content":"As I've read through DA:Fae, I instantly fell in love with it's system and it's lore, feeling a distinct urge to just forget the messiness of Changeling (as many of you probably do too), but still it's hard to find discussions about it.<br /> <br /> As we are probably going to play a Fae campaign in the future. I searched for lists, hints or tips on which dominsions include which types of animals in regard to shapechanging/tranformation.<br /> <br /> They do give a few examples like Dusk including rabbits and singbirds, Day mostly domestic animals, which is comprehensive enough, but Dawn and Night stil aren't clear to me.<br /> <br /> Maybe you can help me thinking of a comprehensive list of sorts (searched for one, unsuccesfully), have one already to help lessen in game discussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13530-queen-nihil","name":"Queen Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13530_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T21:54:35-07:00","id":1151860,"title":"","content":"Dawn: Bees are Matutinal. Rooster, maybe. Many animals that are associated with Dusk can also be used for Dawn as most would be crepuscular. (Active at both Dawn and Dusk). Somer Birds might be Matutinal. Moose and Hyenas are both Crepuscular animals that might fit in Dawn. Hamster.<br /> <br /> Night: Cats, Wolves, Owls. Any Nocturnal Animal or animal people associate with the Night or Winter. So Polar Bear would probably be included. Lynx maybe. Racoons, bats<br /> <br /> Dusk: Rats,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}